---
import PracticeAreaLayout from '../../layouts/PracticeAreaLayout.astro';
---

<PracticeAreaLayout
  title="Small Claims Court Help | Maine Volunteer Lawyers Project"
  description="VLP offers free legal advice for small claims court matters involving disputes under $10,000. Learn about our Small Claims Clinics and how to apply."
  heading="Small Claims Court"
  intro="Free legal advice for disputes under $10,000. VLP volunteer attorneys help you understand procedure, state a proper legal claim, and prepare your defense."
  ctaHeading="Ready to get help with your small claims case?"
  ctaText="Complete an online intake form to request a clinic appointment. VLP staff will review your submission and follow up with you."
>

  <div slot="body">

    <h2>About Small Claims</h2>
    <p>
      The Maine Volunteer Lawyers Project helps litigants with small claims
      court matters, which involve disputes of less than $10,000. Volunteer
      attorneys can help with procedure issues, stating a proper legal claim,
      and understanding how to defend in these matters.
    </p>

    <h2>About This Clinic</h2>

    <div class="notice-box">
      <p>
        Services are free with income-based eligibility. To request an
        appointment, complete the online intake form. A VLP staff member will
        follow up within one to two weeks. If you have an upcoming court date
        or deadline, please note it in your submission.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p>
      Small Claims Clinics are held twice each month on a remote basis  - 
      you can attend by Zoom or by phone. Attorneys can assist with:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Procedural matters and understanding how court works</li>
      <li>Formulating a legitimate legal claim</li>
      <li>Understanding how to defend yourself in a small claims matter</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Additional Resources</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="https://www.courts.maine.gov/help/small-claims/index.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Maine Judicial Branch  -  Small Claims</a>
         -  court forms, process information, and eligibility
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VVN5uP23grk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Video: Going to Small Claims Court in Maine</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://maine.freelegalanswers.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Free Legal Answers Maine</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://ptla.org/self-help/2654" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pine Tree Legal Assistance  -  Self-Help</a>
      </li>
    </ul>

  </div>

  <div slot="sidebar">

    <div class="sidebar-card sidebar-card--info">
      <h3>Eligibility</h3>
      <ul class="sidebar-list">
        <li>Maine legal matter or Maine court</li>
        <li>Limited income (generally at or below 200% of federal poverty level)</li>
        <li>Civil legal matter (not a criminal charge)</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="sidebar-card sidebar-card--info">
      <h3>About This Clinic</h3>
      <ul class="sidebar-list">
        <li>Held twice each month</li>
        <li>Remote  -  Zoom or phone</li>
        <li>Free of charge</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

  </div>

</PracticeAreaLayout>
